    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, i run a small online stationery shop based in lyon and i'm trying to make sure i'm actually following gdpr rules. can u give me a quick summary of the main principles i need to worry about regarding my customers' email addresses and shipping info? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "As a small online shop based in Lyon, you'll need to comply with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) principles. Specifically, you should focus on the \"Lawfulness, Fairness, and Transparency\" (Art. 6) and \"Data Protection by Design and Default\" (Art. 32) principles. For email addresses and shipping info, you should ensure: \n\n1. Consent is explicitly obtained from customers before collecting their data.\n2. Data is processed only for the specific purpose of your services (in this case, shipping and marketing).\n3. You provide clear and transparent information about how data is used and shared.",
